mWizard
=======

motifWizard, abbreviated mWizard, is a lighter, opinionated build of EMWM: a
Motif window manager for the X Window System. Its optional panel is motifWand,
abbreviated mWand.

14mb excluding X server during use.

mWizard is meant for personal use, altho contribution is welcome.

The code in this repo that was added by this project is licensed under MIT license (COPYING.MIT), the rest follows its original LGPL license (COPYING).
See NOTICE for further information.

Documentation is located within doc/ with separate documents for each tool included in this repo.


PREREQUISITES
=============

C99 compliant C compiler
POSIX compliant make

Libraries and headers required for building:

libX11
libXt
libXext
libXrandr
libXinerama
libXm (open-motif/motif)
libXScrnSaver (libXss)

libXss is used only by the idle lock timer. To build without it, remove
-DIDLE_LOCK from DEFINES and -lXss from SYSLIBS in src/common.mf.

Optional at runtime:

stalonetray    system tray, if trayCommand is set
xcursorgen     only to build the cursor theme in goodies

mWand, the optional launcher in mwand/, needs only libX11, libXt and
libXm. It is built separately; see "make mwand" below.


BUILDING AND INSTALLING
=======================

Review the target platform makefile (mf/Makefile.<platform>) and adjust the
installation prefix and X resources path if necessary. The target platform is
picked by the master Makefile from uname(1); if no platform specific makefile
exists, try "Makefile.generic".

    make
    make install        # as root

Additional targets:

    make goodies            unpack and build the extras in goodies/
    make install-goodies    install them (as root)
    make mwand              build mWand, the optional launcher
    make install-mwand      install it (as root)


CONFIGURATION
=============

mWizard reads one file. A sample is installed as PREFIX/X11/system.mwizardrc;
copy it to $HOME/.mwizardrc to customize. It holds key and mouse bindings,
menus, and window manager behaviour in its Settings, Client and Workspace
blocks.

The app-defaults file installed as PREFIX/X11/app-defaults/MWizard carries
appearance only: colors, shadows and fonts.

    doc/CONFIGURATION.md    the full guide, including migration from EMWM
    doc/MWAND.md            configuring mWand
    mwizardrc(4)            rc file syntax
    mwizard(1)              options and appearance resources
